    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n13 Oaklands Drive is a beautifully appointed four-bedroom plus attic family home offering bright spacious accommodation, ideally situated on this mature residential road and just off Serpentine Avenue. The home was recently renovated in 2021.\nBeyond the attractive bay windowed façade, there is a great flow to the accommodation which is presented with a great sense of flair, style and comprises of an entrance hall with guest wc, living room, lounge, open plan kitchen / dining room, study and utility room. Upstairs, there are four bedrooms, main en-suite and a smart family bathroom. The attic has also been converted to a large space with a w.c.\nThe property is set behind a generous landscaped front garden, providing ample off-street parking, a bike storage area and an EV charging point.\nTo the rear, a beautifully landscaped south-facing garden enjoys excellent sunshine throughout the day and into the evening. The garden is laid mainly in lawn with a spacious patio area directly off the kitchen, creating an ideal setting for outdoor dining and entertaining. A standout feature of the garden is the Scandinavian-style barrel sauna, offering the new owners a private wellness and recovery retreat in the comfort of their own home. Beyond the rear boundary lie the grounds of Lansdowne Rugby Club, ensuring an exceptional degree of privacy and feeling of space with no direct overlooking from the rear.\nThe property enjoys one of Dublin's most convenient and popular locations having all of Sandymount's many amenities within walking distance. Sandymount Village, Sandymount Strand, Ballsbridge and Merrion Shopping Centre along with their vast array of coffee shops, restaurants and boutiques are all within easy reach. Some of Dublin's premier schools are all easily accessible, many of which are within walking distance. Public transport is well catered for with Sandymount DART station being closeby. It is also just a short drive from some of Dublin's principle places of business such as Fitzwilliam Square, Merrion Square, Baggot Street and the I.T hub at Grand Canal Dock and Dublin airport is a short drive via the airport tunnel."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nWelcoming entrance hall with polished terrazzo flooring.\n\nOffice - 2.74m x 3.44m\nHome office/study to the front with hardwood flooring, bespoke built-in desk and fitted storage.\n\nGuest WC - \nGuest WC with tiled flooring, wash hand basin and WC.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - 6.52m x 6.21m\nMagnificent open-plan kitchen and dining area featuring polished terrazzo flooring and an extensive range of bespoke fitted units. The kitchen incorporates an integrated fridge freezer, stainless steel sink unit, induction hob, extractor fan and a large island with breakfast bar seating. The bright dining area enjoys wonderful natural light and direct access to the garden.\n\nUtility Room - 1.76m x 3.72m\nWell-appointed utility room plumbed for a washing machine and dryer, with fitted storage units and overhead skylight.\n\nLiving Room - 6.25m x 3.80m\nComfortable living room with hardwood flooring, gas fireplace and TV point.\n\nFamily Room - 3.76m x 3.80m\nElegant principal reception room positioned to the front of the property.\n\nLanding - \nSpacious landing area with carpet flooring.\n\nMain Bedroom - 6.13m x 3.47m\nGenerous double bedroom overlooking the rear garden with floor-to-ceiling glazing, fitted wardrobes and carpet flooring.\n\nEn Suite - 2.21m x 2.55m\nStylish en suite with tiled floor, partially tiled walls, heated towel rail, wash hand basin and WC.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.76m x 3.47m\nLarge double bedroom to the front with bay window and fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.97m x 4.10m\nDouble bedroom overlooking the rear garden with built-in wardrobe and fitted desk.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.73m x 2.71m\nSingle bedroom to the front with built-in wardrobes.\n\nMain Bathroom - 1.62m x 3.22m\nFamily bathroom with tiled flooring, partially tiled walls, bath with shower attachment, wash hand basin, WC and skylight.\n\nAttic Room - 5.00m x 2.98m\nLaid out as a spacious double attic bedroom with carpet flooring, fitted wardrobes and views over the rear garden with w.c.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
